+
+# Spec — R4 forecast flow-shift prediction (Job C)
+
+## Goal
+
+The thundering-herd trap, made legible: when the player considers upgrading a
+pipe's tier, the forecast panel shows the PREDICTED post-upgrade routing BEFORE
+commitment ("traffic will reroute to X" / "equal-cost — flow will split").
+Prediction is a PURE look — never a write, never a sim command.
+
+## Acceptance (from the briefing, pinned as tests)
+
+1. **Predictive helper (core, PURE)** — `core/forecast_shift.odin`:
+   `forecast_shift(t: ^Topology, cat: ^Catalogs, pipe: u32, new_tier: u16,
+   allocator) -> ([dynamic]Route_Shift, Forecast_Error)`. Re-runs Job A's
+   Dijkstra against the hypothetical tier (one shared code path — the
+   honest-prediction construction) and diffs the per-pair next-hop sets.
+   Integer-only, array-only, no rng, no mutation of anything passed in.
+2. **Forecast panel integration** — when a pipe's upgrade is being considered
+   (pipe selected + U key — a view-only look, no command), `app/render/forecast.odin`
+   draws an UPGRADE PREVIEW card: per-kind rows ("N flows reroute to node X",
+   "N flows split — equal cost", "N flows consolidate on node X") + the
+   magnet telegraph ("this upgrade attracts N flows"). Zero pixels when no
+   preview (harness passes nil → existing T2 goldens byte-identical).
+3. **Honest-prediction pin** — core test: helper prediction == actual sim
+   outcome after the upgrade is applied FOR REAL (demolish + redraw at the
+   higher tier through `topology_apply_edit`, the player's real action today),
+   asserted per (from,dst) next-hop set.
+4. **Golden discipline** — NEW demo `forecast_shift.dem` + NEW golden files
+   only; every existing golden must stay byte-identical (harness run green on
+   all demos; any shift = STOP and flag).
+
+## Files
+
+- `core/routing.odin` — extract the Dijkstra body into
+  `routing_rebuild_with_tiers(r, t, cat, tiers: []u16, allocator)`;
+  `routing_rebuild` becomes a one-line wrapper passing `t.pipe_tier[:]`.
+  Behavior byte-identical (tables are derived, never serialized → zero T1
+  impact). Sim path untouched.
+- `core/forecast_shift.odin` (NEW) — `Forecast_Error` (None/Missing_Pipe/
+  Unknown_Tier/Span_Exceeds_Tier), `Shift_Kind` (Reroute/Split/Merge),
+  `Route_Shift{from, dst, kind, old_next, new_next, old_count, new_count,
+  old_pipe, new_pipe}`, `forecast_shift`. Before + after tables built by the
+  SAME `routing_rebuild_with_tiers`; pairs scanned in (from-slot, dst-slot)
+  order; sets equal → no entry.
+- `core/forecast_shift_test.odin` (NEW) — split / reroute / merge geometries
+  (ladder 20/10/5; sums 30/40/25), the honest-prediction pin (real
+  demolish+redraw, table-level equality + flow-level hop assertion), purity
+  (topology byte-unchanged, twice-called determinism), error cases, idempotent
+  no-change.
+- `app/render/forecast.odin` — `Upgrade_Preview{pipe, from_tier, to_tier,
+  shifts: []pp.Route_Shift}`; `draw_forecast_panel(..., preview: ^Upgrade_Preview
+  = nil)`; preview card below the weather card, ASCII-only strings (lint gate 6).
+- `app/main.odin` — `preview_shifts: [dynamic]pp.Route_Shift` (owned) +
+  `preview_active/preview_pipe/preview_to_tier/preview_gen`; U key toggles the
+  preview on the selected pipe (next tier; widest tier → no preview);
+  recompute on (pipe, tier, topology.gen) change; clear on deselect/restart.
+  Never enters the action log.
+- `demos/forecast_shift.dem` (NEW) — two diamonds; the "real upgrade" =
+  demolish + redraw at the higher tier (the player's actual action; no new
+  command per the scope guard). Captures pin pre-upgrade (traffic on the old
+  unique path) + post-upgrade (rerouted / split) behavior. `expect hash stable`.
+- `harness/goldens.odin` — `capture_frame` unchanged (default nil param).
+
+## Verify
+
+`odin test core` green (incl. new pins) · `tools/lint.sh` green ·
+`odin build app -out:app.bin` links · `tools/harness.sh run` all demos green
+(existing goldens byte-identical; forecast_shift new) · drift-check green ·
+launchable increment: select a pipe → U → panel predicts → demolish+redraw →
+the predicted reroute/split happens.
+
+## Scope guard
+
+Prediction ONLY. No auto-routing, no new player sim commands (the preview is
+view-only), no LOG_VERSION change (nothing serialized — flag: derived data),
+no `app/render/view.odin`/`tray.odin` (Job B's ghost/glow files). W2 per-class
+routing preferences remain out. app/main.odin is shared-risk with Job B —
+flagged to Silas in the PR.
