+# forecast_shift.dem — Job C / R4: the forecast flow-shift prediction, proven
+# against the REAL sim. Two compact diamonds (spans 9 <= narrow max 10):
+#   Diamond A (the REROUTE prediction) — ids 0..3:
+#     id 0 = residential res   at (8, 15)  — the source
+#     id 1 = router_basic m1   at (16, 11) — mid router (upper)
+#     id 2 = router_basic m2   at (16, 19) — mid router (lower)
+#     id 3 = content_host host at (24, 15) — the sink
+#     res->m1 STANDARD(10) + m1->host narrow(20) = 30  <- the current unique path
+#     res->m2 narrow(20) + m2->host narrow(20) = 40
+#     THE UPGRADE (the player's real action — demolish + redraw at the higher
+#     tier; no new command): at 1500ms demolish pipe 1 (res->m2 narrow), at
+#     1600ms redraw it WIDE (5). The R4 helper predicts: "traffic will reroute
+#     to node 2 (m2)" — b-side becomes 5+20 = 25 < 30. The 2800ms capture pins
+#     the prediction coming TRUE: post-upgrade packets ride ONLY the m2 legs;
+#     the m1 path carries nothing.
+#   Diamond B (the SPLIT prediction) — ids 4..7:
+#     id 4 = residential res2 at (32, 15)  — the source
+#     id 5 = router_basic r1  at (40, 11)  — mid router (upper)
+#     id 6 = router_basic r2  at (40, 19)  — mid router (lower)
+#     id 7 = content_host host2 at (48, 15) — the sink
+#     res2->r1 standard(10) + r1->host2 narrow(20) = 30 <- the current unique path
+#     res2->r2 narrow(20) + r2->host2 narrow(20) = 40
+#     THE UPGRADE: at 1500ms demolish pipe 5 (res2->r2 narrow), at 1600ms
+#     redraw it STANDARD (10). The R4 helper predicts: "equal-cost — flow will
+#     split" — b-side becomes 10+20 = 30 == 30. The 2800ms capture pins the
+#     tie: packets ride BOTH paths (the pure ECMP hash mod 2 splits them: odd
+#     packet ids -> r1, even -> r2).
+#
+# Transit (FIFO-serialized lane queues — a packet on a shared edge is served
+# in queue order at the edge's capacity: packet_bandwidth 30 -> wide = 1
+# tick/edge, standard = 2, narrow = 6; a packet waits its queue turn):
+#   pre-upgrade wave (ticks 20-23) clears the upper paths by tick 47 — the
+#   2800ms capture's upper-path emptiness is the reroute pin;
+#   post-upgrade: A spawns only at ticks 33-36, so at tick 56 (2800ms) its
+#   last wave is mid-edge on m2->host (deliveries at 41/47/53 clear the queue
+#   ahead of it; the queue never hits the E9 bound); B spawns at ticks 33-36
+#   (deliveries by 55) PLUS a two-packet wave at ticks 48/49 (2400/2450ms) —
+#   the ECMP hash sends tick-48 to r1 and tick-49 to r2, so at tick 56 ONE
+#   packet is mid-edge on EACH narrow leg: the split, both paths live.
+# The predictions themselves are pinned by core/forecast_shift_test.odin (the
+# honest-prediction pin asserts helper == sim table); this demo + `expect hash
+# stable` pin the REAL post-upgrade behavior + its replay determinism.
+seed 42
+run 2900ms
+fixture off
+spawn_node residential 8 15
+spawn_node router_basic 16 11
+spawn_node router_basic 16 19
+spawn_node content_host 24 15
+spawn_node residential 32 15
+spawn_node router_basic 40 11
+spawn_node router_basic 40 19
+spawn_node content_host 48 15
+at 500ms draw 0 1 standard
+at 500ms draw 0 2 narrow
+at 500ms draw 1 3 narrow
+at 500ms draw 2 3 narrow
+at 500ms draw 4 5 standard
+at 500ms draw 4 6 narrow
+at 500ms draw 5 7 narrow
+at 500ms draw 6 7 narrow
+at 1000ms spawn 0 3
+at 1050ms spawn 0 3
+at 1100ms spawn 0 3
+at 1150ms spawn 0 3
+at 1000ms spawn 4 7
+at 1050ms spawn 4 7
+at 1100ms spawn 4 7
+at 1150ms spawn 4 7
+capture at 1300ms
+at 1500ms demolish pipe 1
+at 1500ms demolish pipe 5
+at 1600ms draw 0 2 wide
+at 1600ms draw 4 6 standard
+at 1650ms spawn 0 3
+at 1700ms spawn 0 3
+at 1750ms spawn 0 3
+at 1800ms spawn 0 3
+at 1650ms spawn 4 7
+at 1700ms spawn 4 7
+at 1750ms spawn 4 7
+at 1800ms spawn 4 7
+at 2400ms spawn 4 7
+at 2450ms spawn 4 7
+capture at 2800ms
+expect hash stable
